Title: Moral Dilemma
Structure: sequence

            >FADE IN:

# The Warning

[[id: q1]]

[[goal: warn | id: warn | subject: NARRATOR | object: the viewer]]

= A narrator from one possible future sets out to warn us.

.INT. GAME SHOW SET - DAY

[[id: s1]]

Static engulfs the screen. As it comes into focus, a game show TV set with a red box on the floor for the contestant to stand, a plastic wall behind them with the logo of "Moral Dilemma," and a picture of a very well-dressed man.

!Static ripples across the screen.

.INT. GAME SHOW SET - CONTINUOUS

[[id: s2]]

A game show TV set with a red box on the floor for the contestant to stand, a plastic wall behind them with the logo of "Moral Dilemma," and a picture of a very well-dressed man.

[[beat: The Narrator gets our attention | id: b1 | ahead: NARRATOR]]

!NARRATOR stands looking straight at the audience and knocks on the screen.

                NARRATOR
    Hello. What you are about to witness... hasn't happened yet. This is but one possible future—a world where overpopulation and scarcity have pushed humanity to desperate measures.

Insert a series of quick visuals: barren supermarkets, overcrowded urban streets, and fields of dead crops under a gray sky. The visuals are harsh and unforgiving.

                NARRATOR (V.O.)
    Food is running out, and resources are dwindling, forcing societies to embrace extreme solutions. In this grim reality, morality has become entertainment, and life-and-death decisions are made for the sake of ratings.

            >THE CAMERA SHIFTS BACK TO THE GAME SHOW SET.:

The scrolling faces on the plexiglass screen become sharper and more unsettling, each one paired with a numeric value, hinting at the currency of human relationships.

                NARRATOR
    Welcome to *Moral Dilemma*, the brainchild of the enigmatic Archibald Feinious Duke. Here, contestants can trade the _lives_ of those they love for cold, hard cash. The more valuable the relationship, the greater the prize—but at what cost?

The screen flickers with static, creating a ripple effect as if the broadcast is distorting. The world of the game show seems to bleed into the present day, giving the impression that something unnatural is occurring.

                NARRATOR
    "Ahh, the theme song. This show answers the age-old question: 'What is a relationship really worth?'”

[[beat: He turns it on the viewer | id: b42 | ahead: NARRATOR]]

!Narrator listens to the music for a second. The narrator looks at the board.

                NARRATOR
    See anyone you know?

Screen flickers with static, creating a ripple effect as if the broadcast is distorting. The world of the game show seems to bleed into the present day, giving the impression that something unnatural is occurring.

!Narrator hits the camera. Static clears up.

                NARRATOR
    You may wonder: how is this future reaching you, here and now? (considers) or should I say there and then? Perhaps it's a warning, or maybe... just a glimpse of what could be. We have twisted the threads of time so you are now witnesses to this harrowing spectacle.

The camera zooms out, revealing the set in its entirety, the lights flashing in anticipation of the show’s beginning.

                NARRATOR
    So, dear viewer, brace yourself. Ask not what others are worth... but what price you would put on love. Because in this world, everything—even relationships—has a price tag. This show answers the age-old question - "What is a relationship really worth?"

!Static across the screen.

            >RESOLVE TO THE LICENSE PLATE OF A FUTURISTIC CAR:

# The Boyfriend

