[[id: s5]]

The game show set consists of a red outlined box on the floor and an electronic plexiglass screen behind the box.

ARCHIBALD joins the scene from Stage Right.

SUZIE, 20s, stands in the Red Box, clapping along with the audience.

[[beat: Archibald turns to Suzie | id: b8 | ahead: ARCHIBALD]]

[[goal: win | id: money | subject: SUZIE | object: the record payout]]

                ARCHIBALD
    Welcome back to another exciting episode of Moral Dilemma. Last time, we ran out of time before our contestant could finish. Everyone remembers the beautiful Suzie. Welcome back, Suzie.

!Audience Applause

                SUZIE
    Thank you, Mr. Duke.

                ARCHIBALD
    Oh, call me Archibald. Everyone does. Except the recently departed. They don't really say anything.

!Audience laughs

                SUZIE
        (star-struck)
    Ok. Archibald.

                ARCHIBALD
    Let see what has happened thus far. You were only able to pick one victim.

!A picture of PHILLIS smiling in a Pilates outfit shows on screen.

                ARCHIBALD
    You picked your Pilates instructor Phillis.

                SUZIE
    She always said hello to me and always made these little biscuits.

!Picture changes to Phillis holding out some small biscuits.

                ARCHIBALD
    We offered you thirteen thousand, and you took it. And it's a good thing because she has since been arrested for tax evasion. We all know what that means.

!Picture changes to Phillis being taking away from PAB solders

!Archibald pan mime a noose. Audience laughs.

                ARCHIBALD
    Thomas, tell our first-time viewers how this game works.

!INSERT - AUTOMATION of the AI program working.

                NARRATOR (O.S.)
    The Moral Dilemma's Artificial Intelligence receives information from many places: social media, emails, even surveillance cameras. And brings it all together to equate the value of a relationship. Each contestant must decide if they know their relationships better than the computer. If they do, they win lots of my money. But if they don't, they just might go home empty handed. The game ends when one contestant loses twice or decide to let the victim live.

!BACK TO SCENE

                ARCHIBALD
    In the case of your Pilates instructor, you decided to keep the original offer and not watch the evidence. If you had, it would have gone down to 1200 dollars. You were pretty lucky.

[[beat: Suzie wins the room | id: b43 | ahead: SUZIE]]

                SUZIE
    That wasn't luck! It's game strategy. I'm betting my life on this game. I am a relationship-making machine! I make friends literally everywhere I go.

                ARCHIBALD
    It sounds like you have been giving this a lot of thought!

                SUZIE
*    You never know what someone will be worth!* Am I right?

                AUDIENCE (O.C.)
    RIGHT!

                SUZIE
    I look at it that if I didn't get on the show, I got many people who can help me move! However, if THE Archibald comes to a knocking, I can turn them into cash!

                ARCHIBALD
    Into what?

                SUZIE
        (shouts)
    CASH!

                ARCHIBALD
    Well... Audience. Do we like Suzie?

!The audience gives a big cheer.

                ARCHIBALD
    Do we REALLY like her?

!The audience gives an even bigger cheer.

                ARCHIBALD
    Well, I like you too. In fact...

!Suzie fidgets.

                ARCHIBALD
    Thomas, add another potential victim. Let's get this girl some Money!

!Four Squares appear on the screen behind Suzie. They have the letters "A", "B", "C", and "D" as well as the image of Phillis.

                ARCHIBALD
    You will be able to pick from these victims. I'll tell you a little secret. One of these has the opportunity to be the largest bounty we have EVER given out.o

!The audience lets out a lot of glee and hoots.

                SUZIE
        (shocked)
    The largest... ever?

                ARCHIBALD
    Yes. But the other two have some of the lowest. Are you ready to choose?

                SUZIE
    Hmm

!The audience is shouting out letters... A, C, D, B, G.

                ARCHIBALD
    G? There ain't no G!

!Suzie is intensely studying the choices.

                ARCHIBALD
    No pressure, but our biggest payout ever could be waiting for you.

                AUDIENCE
        (shouts)
    C.

                ARCHIBALD
    I need a decision. The crowd seems to like C.

                SUZIE
    I pick B. B as in Boy.

                ARCHIBALD
    Okay! Let's see B.

[[beat: Durand goes on the block | id: b44 | ahead: SUZIE]]

[[goal: cash in | id: durand | subject: SUZIE | object: DURAND | for: money]]

!The B is revealed and DURAND, handsome late 20s., is there. Suzie is enthusiastically dancing around.

                ARCHIBALD
    Who is that, Suzie?

                SUZIE
    That's my Durand. My boyfriend!

                ARCHIBALD
    A boyfriend. You think that a boyfriend might be worth some Cash!

                SUZIE
    Well, I know that he bought a ring. And that he has a good job.

                ARCHIBALD
    Wait a minute. How do you know that he bought a ring?

                SUZIE
        (conspiratorial)
    Well, I have spies.

                ARCHIBALD
    Well... He is worth 45,000 dollars right now. No questions asked.

!Audience applause

                ARCHIBALD
    But before you answer.

                SUZIE
    Yes...

                ARCHIBALD
    On this show, what do you call a man that buys you a ring?

                SUZIE
        (thinks hard)
    Um.. a cash machine?

!Audience laughs.

                ARCHIBALD
    We broke into a security camera, and its video might add a lot of sugar to the pot or turn it sour. Do you take a risk and watch it or take the 45 thousand?

                SUZIE
    Can I see a sample?

                ARCHIBALD
    Thomas, give her a taste.

focuses on the victim board

